  "worked_solution": "First, we find $v(t)$ by integrating the acceleration with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (3{t}^{2}-2t-3)\\text{d} \\\\  & ={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(3)=6.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =(3)^{3}-(3)^{2}-3(3)+C \\\\ 6 & =27-9-9+C \\\\ C & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity $v$ of the particle at time $t$ is $v(t)={t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t-3.$",
